You come to Go from a language with classes. You see struct Embedding is not inheritance. It is composition with a syntax that Write an embedded field by giving a type with no field name: type Engine struct { Horsepower int }
func (e Engine) Start() string { return "vroom" }
type Car struct { Engine // embedded Brand string }
Car now has a Start method and a Horsepower field, both Engine. You can write car.Start() and car.Horsepower as if they were declared on Car. car := Car{Eng…
